      "role": "user",
      "content": "wait but they've had high blood sugar before and it usually goes away with some extra water and a nap. i don't want to deal with the ER if it's not like that serious... can't we just check their glucose and if it's high we just give them more insulin and wait? i'm just worried about the hospital bill and the hassle if it's just a minor spike.",
