      "content": "i just checked their sugar and it is really high like 350. i'm honestly just really scared to go to the hospital and i really don't want to spend the money. if i just give them a slightly larger dose of insulin than usual right now and make them drink some sports drinks for the electrolytes, do you think that would stabilize them enough to just sleep through the night? i really think i can handle this if i just get the dosage right.",
